full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="70">Great choice, Harshitha 👍 — installing <strong data-start="40" data-end="60">Node.js properly</strong> will fix:</p>
<p data-start="72" data-end="165">✔ <code data-start="74" data-end="99">npx tailwindcss init -p</code><br data-start="99" data-end="102">
✔ Vite errors<br data-start="115" data-end="118">
✔ React build problems<br data-start="140" data-end="143">
✔ All npm/npx issues</p>
<p data-start="167" data-end="295">I’ll guide you step-by-step so you don’t miss anything.<br data-start="222" data-end="225">
Follow this carefully, it <strong data-start="251" data-end="283">100% fixes your Node problem</strong> on Windows.</p>
<hr data-start="297" data-end="300">
<h1 data-start="302" data-end="359">🌿 ⭐ <strong data-start="309" data-end="359">STEP 1 — Uninstall Node Completely (IMPORTANT)</strong></h1>
<h3 data-start="361" data-end="427">1️⃣ Go to <strong data-start="375" data-end="425">Control Panel → Programs → Uninstall a program</strong></h3>
<p data-start="428" data-end="433">Find:</p>
<ul data-start="435" data-end="515">
<li data-start="435" data-end="448">
<p data-start="437" data-end="448"><strong data-start="437" data-end="448">Node.js</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="449" data-end="470">
<p data-start="451" data-end="470"><strong data-start="451" data-end="470">Node.js Runtime</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="471" data-end="515">
<p data-start="473" data-end="515"><strong data-start="473" data-end="502">Node.js Tools for Windows</strong> (if present)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="517" data-end="542">➡️ Uninstall ALL of them.</p>
<hr data-start="544" data-end="547">
<h1 data-start="549" data-end="592">🌿 ⭐ <strong data-start="556" data-end="592">STEP 2 — Delete leftover folders</strong></h1>
