6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-bash"><span><span>npm run dev
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
</li>
<li data-start="10301" data-end="10373">
<p data-start="10304" data-end="10373">Open a plant that has a <code data-start="10328" data-end="10335">model</code> field. The 3D viewer should appear.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="10374" data-end="10516">
<p data-start="10377" data-end="10397">On Android (Chrome):</p>
<ul data-start="10401" data-end="10516">
<li data-start="10401" data-end="10516">
<p data-start="10403" data-end="10516">If Scene Viewer / WebXR is available, the viewer shows an AR icon. Tap it to place the plant in real environment.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="10517" data-end="10631">
<p data-start="10520" data-end="10536">On iOS (Safari):</p>
<ul data-start="10540" data-end="10631">
<li data-start="10540" data-end="10631">
<p data-start="10542" data-end="10631">If you have <code data-start="10554" data-end="10561">.usdz</code> and <code data-start="10566" data-end="10575">ios-src</code> is set, tapping the AR/quik-look icon opens Quick Look.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="10633" data-end="10760">If the AR icon does not show, your device might not support WebXR / Scene Viewer; still test the 3D viewer in desktop browsers.</p>
<hr data-start="10762" data-end="10765">
<h2 data-start="10767" data-end="10822">8) Small UX polish suggestions (easy wins for marks)</h2>
<ul data-start="10824" data-end="11167">
<li data-start="10824" data-end="10903">
<p data-start="10826" data-end="10903">Add a simple caption under the model with “Drag to rotate / Pinch to zoom”.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="10904" data-end="11000">
<p data-start="10906" data-end="11000">Show a small “AR supported” indicator if both <code data-start="10952" data-end="10959">model</code> and <code data-start="10964" data-end="10968">ar</code> are available for that plant.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="11001" data-end="11076">
<p data-start="11003" data-end="11076">Provide a fallback static image if 3D fails to load (handle <code data-start="11063" data-end="11072">onError</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="11077" data-end="11167">
<p data-start="11079" data-end="11167">Add attribution or source link for each 3D model in the References section of the modal.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="11169" data-end="11172">
<h2 data-start="11174" data-end="11278">9) Example: full PlantDetailModal snippet (paste to replace the existing component in your <code data-start="11268" data-end="11277">App.jsx</code>)</h2>
<p data-start="11280" data-end="11367">Below is the full modal component ready to paste (it includes the <code data-start="11346" data-end="11360">model-viewer</code> code):</p>
