</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="1208" data-end="1239">with the actual JSX, not <code data-start="1233" data-end="1238">...</code>.</p>
<p data-start="1241" data-end="1291">❗ Using <code data-start="1249" data-end="1254">...</code> inside JSX always causes blank page.</p>
<hr data-start="1293" data-end="1296">
<h1 data-start="1298" data-end="1363">✅ <strong data-start="1302" data-end="1363">STEP 4 — Check if you placed the PLANTS array ABOVE App()</strong></h1>
<p data-start="1364" data-end="1432">Your PLANTS array <strong data-start="1382" data-end="1405">must be above App()</strong>, not inside any component.</p>
<p data-start="1434" data-end="1515">If you accidentally placed PLANTS <strong data-start="1468" data-end="1478">inside</strong> another component, React will crash.</p>
<hr data-start="1517" data-end="1520">
<h1 data-start="1522" data-end="1564">✅ <strong data-start="1526" data-end="1564">STEP 5 — Check for missing imports</strong></h1>
