6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-bash"><span><span>npm install @google/model-viewer
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="14464" data-end="14593">Make sure an import exists somewhere loaded at app startup (we included it in the modal file):<br data-start="14558" data-end="14561">
<code data-start="14561" data-end="14593">import "@google/model-viewer";</code></p>
<hr data-start="14595" data-end="14598">
<h2 data-start="14600" data-end="14628">8) Where to put 3D models</h2>
<p data-start="14629" data-end="14799">Create folder <code data-start="14643" data-end="14666">client/public/models/</code> and place GLB files named like <code data-start="14698" data-end="14709">tulsi.glb</code>, <code data-start="14711" data-end="14728">ashwagandha.glb</code> etc. If you don't have GLB yet, the UI will show the fallback message.</p>
<hr data-start="14801" data-end="14804">
<h2 data-start="14806" data-end="14822">9) How to run</h2>
<p data-start="14823" data-end="14837">From <code data-start="14828" data-end="14836">client</code>:</p>
