role="assistant" data-message-id="a96ae808-421a-4b07-a680-3e1b1a6e7b68" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-t-mini"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="488">Great — I’ll give you a polished, <strong data-start="34" data-end="68">enhanced &amp; innovative frontend</strong> for your <strong data-start="78" data-end="103">Virtual Herbal Garden</strong> (AYUSH — Ayurveda, Yoga &amp; Naturopathy, Unani, Siddha, Homeopathy).<br data-start="170" data-end="173">
Drop these files into <code data-start="195" data-end="208">client/src/</code> (and <code data-start="214" data-end="223">client/</code> root for Tailwind config). I’ll also list the exact npm installs and where to put model/audio assets. This frontend is ready for a <strong data-start="355" data-end="368">200-marks</strong> project: 3D scene, zone navigation, AR/3D viewer, audio guides, quizzes, responsive UI, accessibility-ready components.</p>
<hr data-start="490" data-end="493">
<h1 data-start="495" data-end="527">What you’ll get (files to add)</h1>
<p data-start="528" data-end="564">Place the following under <code data-start="554" data-end="563">client/</code>:</p>
<ul data-start="566" data-end="1084">
<li data-start="566" data-end="584">
<p data-start="568" data-end="584"><code data-start="568" data-end="582">src/main.jsx</code></p>
</li>
