</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="302" data-end="420">This error <strong data-start="313" data-end="344">does NOT come from Tailwind</strong>.<br data-start="345" data-end="348">
It comes from <strong data-start="362" data-end="398">a corrupted Node.js installation</strong> or <strong data-start="402" data-end="419">path conflict</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="422" data-end="544">And because Tailwind is not installed →<br data-start="461" data-end="464">
your UI looks <strong data-start="478" data-end="513">plain, broken, merged, unstyled</strong>, exactly like your screenshot.</p>
<p data-start="546" data-end="617">So, before I give you the enhanced UI,<br data-start="584" data-end="587">
we MUST <strong data-start="595" data-end="616">fix Node.js first</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="619" data-end="622">
<h1 data-start="624" data-end="674">🔥 <strong data-start="629" data-end="674">STEP 1 — COMPLETELY REMOVE BROKEN NODE.JS</strong></h1>
<h3 data-start="676" data-end="719">1️⃣ Uninstall Node from Control Panel</h3>
