</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="183" data-end="324">This happens ONLY when <strong data-start="206" data-end="239">Tailwind is already installed</strong>, OR<br data-start="243" data-end="246">
your project does NOT need the <code data-start="277" data-end="283">init</code> command because the files already exist.</p>
<p data-start="326" data-end="413">So before we do anything else, we need to <strong data-start="368" data-end="412">check whether Tailwind is already set up</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="415" data-end="418">
<h1 data-start="420" data-end="474">✅ STEP 1 — Check if Tailwind config ALREADY exists</h1>
<p data-start="475" data-end="531">Go to the VS Code Explorer and look for these two files:</p>
<p data-start="533" data-end="583">✔ <strong data-start="535" data-end="557">tailwind.config.js</strong><br data-start="557" data-end="560">
✔ <strong data-start="562" data-end="583">postcss.config.js</strong></p>
<p data-start="585" data-end="620">You already showed me earlier that:</p>
<p data-start="622" data-end="717">👉 <code data-start="625" data-end="645">tailwind.config.js</code> exists<br data-start="652" data-end="655">
👉 <code data-start="658" data-end="677">postcss.config.js</code> exists (usually Auto-generated by Vite)</p>
<p data-start="719" data-end="770">💡 <strong data-start="722" data-end="770">If these exist, then you DO NOT need to run:</strong></p>
