lex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="169">Great, Harshitha — that actually makes things <strong data-start="46" data-end="62">much simpler</strong>.<br data-start="63" data-end="66">
If <strong data-start="69" data-end="95">App.css is not present</strong>, then it cannot interfere with Tailwind.<br data-start="136" data-end="139">
So the only thing missing was:</p>
<h3 data-start="171" data-end="196">❗ <code data-start="177" data-end="196">postcss.config.js</code></h3>
<p data-start="198" data-end="249">Once we add this file, Tailwind will start working.</p>
<p data-start="251" data-end="317">Let’s finish this cleanly and correctly. Follow these exact steps:</p>
<hr data-start="319" data-end="322">
<h1 data-start="324" data-end="363">⭐ STEP 1 — CREATE <code data-start="344" data-end="363">postcss.config.js</code></h1>
<p data-start="365" data-end="376">In VS Code:</p>
<h3 data-start="378" data-end="419">✔ Right-click the <strong data-start="400" data-end="410">client</strong> folder</h3>
<h3 data-start="420" data-end="446">✔ Click <strong data-start="432" data-end="444">New File</strong></h3>
<h3 data-start="447" data-end="461">✔ Name it:</h3>
